oday uh the eu proposal  is that it is  that certification includes both whether  you've had the vaccine and also whether  you've recently had a  test for those who can't get vaccinated  yet  um which is obviously uh particularly  important  um i i i i therefore it's  it's it's something that we're working  with them  and others on um and it matters that we  get the details of this right  for international travel and on the  question  on the roadmap um what i'd say in  response to your question  is that we have set out the tests  precisely so  we can be we can be sure  that the data still allow  for the safe step down  the road map and i'm highly confident  that the opening of schools on monday  is the right thing to do and the data  point that way and then we will assess  the data before taking  step two the the roadmap is designed  to be able to see the data before we  take each step  and so we've done it in that way in  order to  be able to have the assurance that we  are taking  a cautious yet irreversible path out of  this  pandemic dr hopkins anything to add on  that well  i would agree i think the thing that we  know is that children going back to  school and  each point is likely to increase  interactions with others  and therefore we are likely to see an  increase in the ore number  and potentially more transmissions what  we need to do is give time after each of  the  events to monitor the impact of that not  just on cases in the community  but particularly on hospital admissions  and deaths which is what  we see that the vaccines are preventing  and what will prevent  surges in hospitalizations and therefore  a big impact  so we'll need to monitor the cases after  each step and that's going to be really  important  thank you secretary of state at the risk  of sounding like a parrot  i'm not worried about any particular  step  i am far more worried that there is time  to consider the effect of each step  before we move on to the next one  and that way we get into a process  where we are hopefully with vaccines  relaxing in a very long-term way  and we don't have to go backwards and  forwards and backwards and forwards  in these kind of stuttering steps i'd  rather take  much slower and more pronounced and  measured steps  that always go in one direction and that  just means  moving a little more slowly than  sometimes  your instincts and your emotions and  your desires  um uh would lead you to want to do  there's one final point i'd like to make  on this uh joel which is the  the link to the data that we just  published on the vaccine efficacy  because the effectiveness of the vaccine  on protecting  people and on reducing transmission  is critical to the roadmap the only  reason we can set out  as full of roadmap as we have is because  of the vaccine rollout  because we know that without the vaccine  uh the uh  the the the the there is no way to keep  people safe in the way that we can with  the vaccine  and so the data that we've published  today  shows that the road map is  achievable because it shows that we will  be able  to break the link from cases through to  hospitalizations  and to deaths and until now in the  pandemic  that link from cases through to  hospitalizations and deaths has been  unbreakable and we have demonstrated  with the data today  that the vaccines can break that link  and that is down to the  power of science so it's good news for  everybody  and in in a way it it's reassuring  for our ability to progress down the  road map
 

